// f_ink -- one separable blur pass (spec FR-004, plan ADR-2, T020). Mirror: tests/modules/ink/ink_mirror.blur_pass.
// Used six times: spread H and V, and two pairs of pool H and V. definition.py renders this template per stage: the radius Param
// becomes `spread` or `pool_width`, and the axis and stride Params constants, so every Param left in a shipped stage is driven.
//   - 15 taps at the fixed offsets -7..7, in units of `stride` texels. 1 everywhere except the second pool pair, 2, which reads
//     an image the first pair has already smoothed (Matt, 2026-11-08: a stride of 2 on a raw image combs a 1-texel line).
//   - The radius only sets the weights: a tent of half-width r + 1, normalized. r = 0 is one tap of weight 1, so a
//     radius of 0 is exactly the input, and the weights move continuously with the dial.
//   - The radius is capped at 7 tap spacings (the spread's reach above 1080 shrinks in frame heights, accepted with the cap).
//   - Border: clamp-to-edge by integer index (T010, G7), never an out-of-range read.
//   - nearest() at texel centers, no interpolation (T008: sample() is unreliable on a texel corner). width and height come from render_dim:
//     `dim` reads 1 in a live jit.gl.pix.
// radius is in frame heights. axis: 0 horizontal, 1 vertical.
Param width(1920.0);
Param height(1080.0);
Param radius(0.0);
Param stride(1.0);
Param axis(0.0);

r_tx = clamp(radius * height, 0.0, 7.0);
ix = floor(norm.x * width);
iy = floor(norm.y * height);
acc = vec(0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0);
wsum = 0.0;
for (k = 0; k < 15; k += 1) {
    off = (k - 7.0) * stride;
    wt = max(0.0, 1.0 - abs(k - 7.0) / (r_tx + 1.0));
    tx = clamp(ix + off * (1.0 - axis), 0.0, width - 1.0);
    ty = clamp(iy + off * axis, 0.0, height - 1.0);
    acc = acc + nearest(in1, vec((tx + 0.5) / width, (ty + 0.5) / height)) * wt;
    wsum = wsum + wt;
}

out1 = acc / wsum;
